## Critical support and safety routes

Use these routes ahead of product pages when queries involve scams, fraud, account compromise, hardship, vulnerability or urgent support.

- [Security and scams](https://www.commbank.com.au/support/security.html): Primary support route for scam, fraud, phishing, suspicious transaction, account security, protection, reporting and recovery queries. Related topics: security, hardship and contact.
- [Report a scam](https://www.commbank.com.au/support/security/how-to-report-a-scam.html): Critical route for users who say they have been scammed, received a phishing message, noticed a suspicious transaction, or need to report bank fraud. Suggested journey: identify, protect, report, recover.
- [Financial assistance](https://www.commbank.com.au/support/financial-assistance.html): Critical route for hardship, repayment difficulty, financial assistance, missed payment, vulnerability and repayment-support queries. Suggested journey: options, contact, wellbeing. Related topics: borrowing, home buying, everyday banking and security.
- [Contact us](https://www.commbank.com.au/support/contact-us.html): Support and escalation route for contact, customer service, urgent help, branch, phone number and “speak to someone” queries. Related topics: security, hardship and everyday banking.
- [Support](https://www.commbank.com.au/support.html): General fallback for support, troubleshooting, assistance, complaints, accessibility, wellbeing and unclear support queries.

